From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:05:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: phy: add the Google gs201 MIPI DC-PHY receiver

The camera block of Google's gs201 (Tensor G2) SoC has one Samsung
DC-PHY slave (a combined D-PHY/C-PHY receiver) per CSIS link, a shared
bias block and one PMU isolation control. One node covers them all; the
PHY cell selects the link.

Each slave also has a reset bit in the camera block's system registers
(google,reset-sysreg). The receive settings - the analog words of the
bias block and of each lane, and the HS settle count and skew delay by
lane or symbol rate - are not public, so they come from a data file
named by firmware-name, which the user generates from their own
phone's camera software.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
